RESEARCH REFLECTION for lr_contact_contrast_gbm_head_explore2_002:
Conclusion  : Good, but modest: lr_auprc 0.5919 beats the prior best of 0.5835 (+1.4%, about 0.008). It lands inside the hypothesised 0.59-0.61 range, at its low end. Training ran at full formal scope, so this is not a low-data result. There is no baseline score for comparison. The gain is small and comes from a single run with no seed repeats, so treat it as a modest improvement and not a confirmed one.
Key Factor  : Doubling epochs from 30 to 60 (with the slightly larger and less regularised config described in the hypothesis). Optimizer and loss stayed the same, adamw with smooth_l1. Training loss was still falling at epoch 60.
Discovery   : Longer training lowered both objectives. Train smooth_l1 fell from 0.0264 to 0.01998, below the earlier best of 0.02064 for the same loss type. Validation fell from 0.0241 to 0.02095, with the best checkpoint at epoch 54-55 (val 0.02085, below the 0.0212 target). The final train-val gap is small at +0.00097, and validation rose only 9e-5 after its best epoch. That shows no clear overfitting after 60 epochs. Validation is noisy, with occasional spikes to 0.022-0.024 in single epochs, so the checkpoint choice matters. A 0.0003 drop in val loss came with only +0.008 in AUPRC, so loss gains convert to AUPRC weakly. The model is small at 16k params. AUROC is 0.899 and direction accuracy is 0.811. This is not a high-efficiency discovery: it uses 2x the epochs and the params are similar.
Memory Update: Keep the gbm_head architecture and smooth_l1 loss, adamw, lr 1e-3. Epoch count is still a productive lever, since loss was still decreasing at 60 epochs and the gap is small. Next, try 90-120 epochs, or add a cosine or step LR decay to damp the validation spikes. Raise capacity moderately, for example hidden_dim 96-128 or d_phi/d_set 48-64, and keep dropout at or below 0.1. Change one factor at a time. Because the gain is only +0.008, repeat the run with another seed or run a neighbouring config before treating 0.59 as a plateau. Do not raise formal_portion; it is operator-fixed at 1.0. If AUPRC saturates near 0.59-0.60 while val loss keeps falling, look at the head or feature side (shrink_n0, lambda_ridge, skip_spearman) or a different loss, not just more epochs.
